---
description: Rules for automation flows and async operations
globs: ["server/**/*.ts", "src/lib/**/*.ts", "src/pages/**/*.{ts,tsx}", "src/hooks/**/*.{ts,tsx}"]
---

Automation rules:
- avoid duplicate triggers, sends, posts, or workflow executions
- make async flows explicit and traceable
- think about retries, partial failures, provider instability, and race conditions
- prefer idempotent behavior when possible
- do not assume third-party APIs are reliable
- keep workflow logic understandable and observable
- do not hide critical automation logic inside UI code unless unavoidable

When modifying automation logic:
- identify trigger, validation, execution, and failure handling
- explain risks briefly if the flow is critical
- prefer small safe fixes before deeper refactors